  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the point be $(h, k)$\r\nThen, $\\left|\\frac{h-2 k+1}{\\sqrt{1^{2}+(-2)^{2}}}\\right|=\\sqrt{5}$\r\n$h-2 k+1=\\pm 5$\r\nAlso, $\\left|\\frac{2 h+3 k-1}{\\sqrt{2^{2}+3^{2}}}\\right|=$\r\n$\\Rightarrow \\quad 2 h+3 k-1=\\pm 13$\r\nOn solving Eqs\r\n(i) and (ii), we get four points So. there are much 4 points.",
